  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "A ray of light along $x+\\sqrt{3}y=\\sqrt{3}$ gets reflected upon reaching $x$-axis, the equation of the reflected ray is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "u5n98",
      "text": "$y=x+\\sqrt{3}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "2idQr",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{3} \\mathrm{y}=\\mathrm{x}-\\sqrt{3}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "oc5Bv",
      "text": "$y=\\sqrt{3} x-\\sqrt{3}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "0aBPl",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{3} y=x-1$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{A} \\equiv(\\sqrt{3}, 0)$\r\nLet, B $(0,1)$\r\n$\\therefore \\mathrm{B}^{\\prime} \\equiv(0,-1)$\r\n$\\therefore$ Equation of $\\mathrm{AB}^{\\prime}: \\frac{\\mathrm{y}-0}{0+1}=\\frac{\\mathrm{x}-\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{3}-0} \\Rightarrow \\sqrt{3} \\mathrm{y}=\\mathrm{x}-\\sqrt{3}$\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/6ToocRo59C-9cnQSlrto454exHR8Pf2dJPUh6dRb8qE.original.fullsize.png\">",
